IMPORT prelude

-- Carriage of Goods by Sea Act 1972 (Singapore) -- when the Hague-Visby Rules govern a shipment (ss 2, 3, Articles I(c), V, X), what
-- the carrier answers for (s 4, Articles III(1), (2), IV(1), (2), (4)), the package limit (Article IV(5)), the time bar and notice of
-- loss (Article III(6), (6bis)), what the bill of lading proves (s 3(5), s 5, Article III(4)), which contract terms survive
-- (Articles III(8), V, VI, VII) and dangerous goods (Article IV(6)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CGSA1972.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; no later amendment is annotated.
-- The Schedule is "The Hague Rules as amended by the Brussels Protocol 1968".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0099 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to -- here, a shipper, a cargo owner
-- or a holder of a bill of lading whose goods are lost or damaged at sea. No scenario has asked a sharper question yet.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Minister's order under s 3(8) converting francs into Singapore dollars (not deposited, so every limit here is in
-- gold francs); the valuation rule of Article IV(5)(b); the shipper's indemnity for inaccurate particulars (Article III(5)) beyond
-- s 5; Article IV bis (servants and agents, tort claims); the "shipped" bill (Article III(7)); s 6 and Articles VIII, IX (other
-- limitation and nuclear laws); and which States are contracting States, which the deposit does not list.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Carriage of Goods by Sea Act 1972`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` a b MEANS IF a GREATER THAN b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` a b MEANS IF a LESS THAN b THEN a ELSE b

DECLARE Document IS ONE OF
    `a bill of lading`
    `a non-negotiable receipt marked as such`
    `a charter party with no bill of lading`
    `no document of title`

DECLARE Cargo IS ONE OF
    `general cargo`
    `cargo stated as carried on deck and so carried`
    `cargo carried on deck without being stated as such`
    `live animals`

DECLARE Shipment HAS
    `document` IS A Document
    `cargo` IS A Cargo
    `shipped from a port in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `between ports in 2 different States` IS A BOOLEAN
    `bill issued in a contracting State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `shipped from a port in a contracting State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract expressly provides that the Rules govern` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `2, 3, Articles I(c), V and X -- when the Rules apply`

-- s 3(1): the Rules "have the force of law". (2): they also have effect where "the port of shipment is a port in Singapore, whether
-- or not the carriage is between ports in 2 different States". (3): nothing applies the Rules to a contract "unless the contract
-- expressly or by implication provides for the issue of a bill of lading or any similar document of title". (4): the Rules have the
-- force of law for (a) a bill of lading whose contract "expressly provides that the Rules govern the contract", and (b) "any receipt
-- which is a non-negotiable document marked as such" whose contract so provides.
-- Article X: the Rules apply to every bill of lading "between ports in 2 different States" if (a) issued in a contracting State,
-- (b) from a port in a contracting State, or (c) the contract provides for the Rules. Article V: "The provisions of these Rules shall
-- not be applicable to charter parties".
GIVEN `the shipment` IS A Shipment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Rules reach the contract` IF
    CONSIDER `the shipment`'s `document`
    WHEN `a bill of lading` THEN
            `the shipment`'s `shipped from a port in Singapore`
        OR  `the shipment`'s `the contract expressly provides that the Rules govern`
        OR  (    `the shipment`'s `between ports in 2 different States`
             AND (`the shipment`'s `bill issued in a contracting State` OR `the shipment`'s `shipped from a port in a contracting State`))
    WHEN `a non-negotiable receipt marked as such` THEN `the shipment`'s `the contract expressly provides that the Rules govern`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Article I(c): "Goods" excludes "live animals and cargo which by the contract of carriage is stated as being carried on deck and is
-- so carried". s 3(6): where the Rules apply by s 3(4) (an express clause) to "deck cargo or live animals", they "have effect as if
-- Article I(c) did not exclude deck cargo and live animals". s 3(7) repeats the two-part definition of deck cargo.
GIVEN `the shipment` IS A Shipment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Rules govern the cargo` IF
        `the Rules reach the contract` `the shipment`
    AND CONSIDER `the shipment`'s `cargo`
        WHEN `general cargo` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `cargo carried on deck without being stated as such` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `the shipment`'s `the contract expressly provides that the Rules govern`

§§ `4, Articles III(1), (2), IV(1), (2), (4) -- what the carrier answers for`

-- s 4: no "absolute undertaking by the carrier of the goods to provide a seaworthy ship" is implied. Article III(1): only "due
-- diligence" to make the ship seaworthy. Article IV(1): no liability for unseaworthiness "unless caused by want of due diligence",
-- and "the burden of proving the exercise of due diligence shall be on the carrier". Article III(2): the carrier "shall properly and
-- carefully load, handle, stow, carry, keep, care for, and discharge the goods". Article IV(2) excepts, among others, (a) "Act,
-- neglect, or default of the master, mariner, pilot, or the servants of the carrier in the navigation or in the management of the
-- ship"; (b) "Fire, unless caused by the actual fault or privity of the carrier"; (c) perils of the sea; (d) Act of God; (j)
-- strikes; (m) inherent vice; (n) insufficiency of packing; (p) latent defects; and (q) any other cause without fault, "but the
-- burden of proof shall be on the person claiming the benefit of this exception". Article IV(4): "any reasonable deviation" is not
-- a breach.
DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
    `negligent navigation by the crew`
    `fire without the carrier's actual fault or privity`
    `fire caused by the carrier's actual fault or privity`
    `perils of the sea`
    `act of God`
    `strikes`
    `insufficient packing`
    `inherent vice of the goods`
    `latent defect not discoverable by due diligence`
    `reasonable deviation`
    `unseaworthiness`
    `careless stowage`
    `an otherwise unexplained cause`

GIVEN `the cause` IS A Cause, `the carrier proved due diligence on seaworthiness` IS A BOOLEAN, `the carrier proved no fault of its own or its servants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier is liable for the loss` IF
    CONSIDER `the cause`
    WHEN `fire caused by the carrier's actual fault or privity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `careless stowage` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `unseaworthiness` THEN NOT `the carrier proved due diligence on seaworthiness`
    WHEN `an otherwise unexplained cause` THEN NOT `the carrier proved no fault of its own or its servants`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Article IV(5) -- the package limit`

-- (a): unless "the nature and value of such goods have been declared by the shipper before shipment and inserted in the bill of
-- lading", the carrier is not liable "in an amount exceeding the equivalent of 10,000 francs per package or unit or 30 francs per kilo
-- of gross weight of the goods lost or damaged, whichever is the higher". (c): for a container or pallet, "the number of packages or
-- units enumerated in the bill of lading as packed in such article of transport shall be deemed the number of packages"; "Except as
-- aforesaid such article of transport shall be considered the package or unit". (e): no limit where the damage "resulted from an act
-- or omission of the carrier done with intent to cause damage, or recklessly and with knowledge that damage would probably result".
-- (g): a higher maximum may be agreed, but none "less than the appropriate maximum". (h): no liability "in any event" if the nature
-- or value "has been knowingly mis-stated by the shipper in the bill of lading".
GIVEN `a container or pallet was used` IS A BOOLEAN, `packages enumerated in the bill as packed in it` IS A NUMBER, `packages shipped` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the packages counted for the limit` MEANS
    IF `a container or pallet was used`
    THEN (IF `packages enumerated in the bill as packed in it` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `packages enumerated in the bill as packed in it` ELSE 1)
    ELSE `packages shipped`

GIVEN `packages` IS A NUMBER, `gross kilos` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Rules limit in francs` MEANS
    `the greater of` (`packages` TIMES 10000) (`gross kilos` TIMES 30)

DECLARE Claim HAS
    `loss in francs` IS A NUMBER
    `packages counted` IS A NUMBER
    `gross kilos lost or damaged` IS A NUMBER
    `nature and value declared and inserted in the bill` IS A BOOLEAN
    `agreed maximum in francs` IS A NUMBER
    `carrier acted with intent or recklessly knowing damage was probable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `shipper knowingly mis-stated nature or value in the bill` IS A BOOLEAN

-- An agreed maximum below the Rules limit is ignored (g), and Article III(8) voids any clause "lessening such liability otherwise
-- than as provided in these Rules".
GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum in francs` MEANS
    `the greater of` (`the Rules limit in francs` (`the claim`'s `packages counted`) (`the claim`'s `gross kilos lost or damaged`))
                     (`the claim`'s `agreed maximum in francs`)

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount recoverable in francs` MEANS
    IF `the claim`'s `shipper knowingly mis-stated nature or value in the bill`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the claim`'s `nature and value declared and inserted in the bill`
            OR `the claim`'s `carrier acted with intent or recklessly knowing damage was probable`
         THEN `the claim`'s `loss in francs`
         ELSE `the lesser of` (`the claim`'s `loss in francs`) (`the maximum in francs` `the claim`)

§§ `Article III(6), (6bis) -- notice and time bar`

-- III(6): unless written notice of loss is given "before or at the time of the removal of the goods" or, "if the loss or damage be
-- not apparent, within 3 days", "such removal shall be prima facie evidence of the delivery by the carrier of the goods as described
-- in the bill of lading". "The notice in writing need not be given if the state of the goods has, at the time of their receipt, been
-- the subject of joint survey or inspection." (Treating a joint survey as displacing the presumption is an inference.)
GIVEN `the loss was apparent` IS A BOOLEAN, `written notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN, `days after removal the notice was given` IS A NUMBER, `there was a joint survey` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `removal is prima facie evidence of delivery as described` IF
        (NOT `there was a joint survey`)
    AND (NOT (    `written notice was given`
              AND (    (`the loss was apparent` AND `days after removal the notice was given` AT MOST 0)
                   OR  ((NOT `the loss was apparent`) AND `days after removal the notice was given` AT MOST 3))))

-- III(6): the carrier and ship are "discharged from all liability whatsoever in respect of the goods, unless suit is brought within
-- one year of their delivery or of the date when they should have been delivered. This period may, however, be extended if the
-- parties so agree after the cause of action has risen." (Counting the year as 12 whole months is an inference.)
GIVEN `months from delivery to suit` IS A NUMBER, `extension in months` IS A NUMBER, `extension agreed after the cause of action arose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suit is in time` IF
        `months from delivery to suit` AT MOST 12
    OR  (`extension agreed after the cause of action arose` AND `months from delivery to suit` AT MOST 12 PLUS `extension in months`)

-- III(6bis): an action for indemnity against a third person may be brought after the year "if brought within the time allowed by the
-- law of the Court seized of the case. However, the time allowed shall be not less than 3 months, commencing from the day when the
-- person bringing such action for indemnity has settled the claim or has been served with process".
GIVEN `months since settling or being served` IS A NUMBER, `months allowed by the law of the court` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the indemnity action is in time` IF
    `months since settling or being served` AT MOST `the greater of` `months allowed by the law of the court` 3

§§ `3(5), 5, Article III(4) -- what the bill proves about the goods`

-- III(4): the bill "shall be prima facie evidence of the receipt by the carrier of the goods as therein described. However, proof to
-- the contrary shall not be admissible when the bill of lading has been transferred to a third party acting in good faith." s 3(5):
-- for a non-negotiable receipt brought in by s 3(4)(b), "the second sentence of paragraph 4 of Article III" is omitted. s 5: where
-- by trade custom the weight of bulk cargo "is a weight ascertained or accepted by a third party other than the carrier or the
-- shipper" and the bill says so, "despite anything in the Rules, the bill of lading is not to be deemed to be prima facie evidence
-- against the carrier", nor is the weight "deemed to have been guaranteed by the shipper".
DECLARE `Weight evidence` IS ONE OF
    `no presumption`
    `prima facie evidence`
    `conclusive evidence`

GIVEN `the document` IS A Document, `bulk weight taken by a third party and so stated` IS A BOOLEAN, `held by a third party in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Weight evidence`
`what the stated weight proves against the carrier` MEANS
    IF `bulk weight taken by a third party and so stated`
    THEN `no presumption`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the document`
         WHEN `a bill of lading` THEN (IF `held by a third party in good faith` THEN `conclusive evidence` ELSE `prima facie evidence`)
         WHEN `a non-negotiable receipt marked as such` THEN `prima facie evidence`
         OTHERWISE `no presumption`

GIVEN `bulk weight taken by a third party and so stated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the shipper is deemed to guarantee the weight` IF
    NOT `bulk weight taken by a third party and so stated`

§§ `Articles III(8), V, VI, VII -- which contract terms survive`

-- III(8): a clause "relieving the carrier or the ship from liability for loss or damage ... arising from negligence, fault, or
-- failure in the duties and obligations provided in this article or lessening such liability otherwise than as provided in these
-- Rules, shall be null and void". "A benefit of insurance in favour of the carrier or similar clause shall be deemed to be a clause
-- relieving the carrier from liability." V: the carrier may surrender rights or increase responsibilities, "provided such surrender
-- or increase shall be embodied in the bill of lading", and a "lawful provision regarding general average" may be inserted. VII:
-- the parties may agree anything about the period "prior to the loading on, and subsequent to the discharge from, the ship".
DECLARE Clause IS ONE OF
    `excluding liability for negligent care of the cargo`
    `giving the carrier the benefit of the cargo insurance`
    `lowering the limit below the Rules`
    `raising the carrier's liability above the Rules`
    `excluding liability before loading or after discharge`
    `providing for general average`

-- VI: "any agreement in any terms" is allowed "provided that in this case no bill of lading has been or shall be issued and that the
-- terms agreed shall be embodied in a receipt which shall be a non-negotiable document and shall be marked as such", but not for
-- "ordinary commercial shipments made in the ordinary course of trade", only where the circumstances "are such as reasonably to
-- justify a special agreement".
GIVEN `a bill of lading is issued` IS A BOOLEAN, `terms in a receipt marked non-negotiable` IS A BOOLEAN, `an ordinary commercial shipment` IS A BOOLEAN, `circumstances reasonably justify a special agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a valid Article VI special agreement` IF
        (NOT `a bill of lading is issued`)
    AND `terms in a receipt marked non-negotiable`
    AND (NOT `an ordinary commercial shipment`)
    AND `circumstances reasonably justify a special agreement`

GIVEN `the clause` IS A Clause, `embodied in the bill of lading` IS A BOOLEAN, `under a valid special agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the clause is effective` IF
        `under a valid special agreement`
    OR  CONSIDER `the clause`
        WHEN `raising the carrier's liability above the Rules` THEN `embodied in the bill of lading`
        WHEN `excluding liability before loading or after discharge` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `providing for general average` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Article IV(6) -- dangerous goods`

-- IV(6): dangerous goods "to the shipment whereof the carrier ... has not consented with knowledge of their nature and character, may
-- at any time before discharge be landed at any place, or destroyed or rendered innocuous by the carrier without compensation and the
-- shipper of such goods shall be liable for all damages and expenses". If shipped "with such knowledge and consent" and they "become
-- a danger to the ship or cargo", they may be dealt with "in like manner ... without liability on the part of the carrier except to
-- general average".
GIVEN `the carrier knowingly consented` IS A BOOLEAN, `the goods became a danger` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier may land or destroy the goods` IF
    (NOT `the carrier knowingly consented`) OR `the goods became a danger`

GIVEN `the carrier knowingly consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the shipper is liable for all resulting damages` IF
    NOT `the carrier knowingly consented`
